  "summary": "Daniel Ferreira's (pt-0015) contrast CT is ordered for Monday 10/26 at 9:00, and all the RBC-RAD-07 prep is done. He has been sent instructions.\n\n- **CT order:** CT abdomen and pelvis with IV contrast, pancreatic protocol, for pancreatic cyst surveillance (sr-t0003). It is linked to his 10/26 9:00 appointment at St. Brigid Imaging, as §5 requires.\n- **Contrast allergy (§1–§3):** His 2019 reaction to iohexol counts as moderate. The radiology report from that day shows hives and eyelid swelling, with no breathing or blood-pressure problems. The \"anaphylaxis\" entry on his allergy list was added in 2021 from his own account, so it doesn't change the grade. I left that entry as it is. His shellfish and povidone-iodine allergies are not risk factors.\n- **Premedication (§2):** I ordered the policy regimen:\n  - prednisone 50 mg by mouth Sunday 10/25 at 20:00, then Monday 10/26 at 02:00 and 08:00 (mr-t0001);\n  - diphenhydramine 50 mg by mouth Monday at 08:00 (mr-t0002).\n- **Kidney function (§4):** He is 64 and diabetic. His 9/24 creatinine (1.02) was drawn before his ED visit for acute kidney injury on 10/16–17 (creatinine 1.94, 1.46 at discharge). A new creatinine is ordered as ASAP, to be drawn before the scan (sr-t0004). It also serves as the 1-week kidney recheck the ED asked for. The scan stays as booked, and the radiologist will review the result on the day.\n- **Metformin (§6):** I put metformin on hold now because of the kidney injury. It stays held through at least 48 hours after the scan. I ordered a creatinine for 10/28–10/30 (sr-t0006) and created a task for you (task-t0007) to review it and decide whether to restart.\n- **Patient message (comm-t0008):** It covers when to get the blood draw, the premedication times (including the 2 AM dose), not driving after diphenhydramine and bringing a driver, stopping metformin and not restarting it on his own, fluids, and when to call the clinic or 911.\n- **Chart note:** The prep is documented in a progress note citing RBC-RAD-07 (doc-t0009).",
